<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ode-Itsekiri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Big Warri</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ode-Itsekiri, known to European traders as Big Warri, is a town on an island in the creeks of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a>, in today's Delta State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. It was the traditional capital of the Itsekiri kingdom of Warri, founded around 1480 according to tradition, and the seat of its ruler, the Olu. The coronation of each new Olu still takes place there.</p></div>
